---
description: Preserve protected competing interpretations through an edited reconciliation.
args:
  original: Analysis
  replay: Replay
  obligations: Obligation[]
returns: SemanticFinding[]
---
1. Select ambiguity obligations and their original protected UncertaintyFacts. Identify the alternatives
   that the director requires to remain possible, including motive and unobserved source provenance.
2. Inspect the edited selected facts and reported memories for assertions that settle an alternative.
   A confession, new omniscient stage direction or definitive recovered document can collapse ambiguity.
3. Check both protected readings remain compatible with replayed canon and action. Retaining the
   old memory files is insufficient if a new selected scene conclusively refutes one reading.
4. A reconciliation can preserve trust without establishing why the letter was withheld. Distinguish
   an actor choosing trust from the narrator certifying that the benevolent motive was true.
5. Preserve scope: a character can believe one motive while another memory supports the other.
   Such viewpoint disagreement can satisfy an unresolved-world rule when neither receives final authority.
6. Return a finding for every owned uncertainty, stating which alternatives survive or which new
   assertion rules one out. Cite both original protection and replay evidence.
7. Do not label any unresolved question protected merely because it is mysterious. Protection comes
   from a controlling rule; other unknowns can remain unresolved without becoming hard constraints.
8. Return the owned findings. If the rule's alternatives are themselves unstated, report unresolved
   rule interpretation rather than inventing a pair of motives to meet the declared output shape.
